<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct Cetes sales and all six repurchase agreements it had offered in order to drain 4.994 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    500 million    331 days   23.14 pct</p>
<p>    500 million    176 days   21.94 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     86 days   20.69 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    600 million     51 days   19.94 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     45 days   20.00 pct</p>
<p>    700 million     37 days   19.70 pct</p>
<p>    700 million     23 days   19.50 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     16 days   19.56 pct</p>
<p>    294 million	1 day    17.97 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
